<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asantehene</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Asantehene is the title of the king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a>, the ruler of the Ashanti Empire. The office was established by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osei-tutu-i">Osei Tutu</a> around the end of the seventeenth century and symbolised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-stool">Golden Stool</a>, the sacred throne of the nation. The Asantehene governed with a council of chiefs and remains a traditional ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> today.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asantehene.jpg" alt="Asantehene" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kofi oo Kofi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otumfuo-osei-tutu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
